# Review

## Summary

A one-paragraph rewrite would lose real content. The note does more than restate one insight. It separates admission from ranking, lays out five valuation lenses that each have a different test and a different point at which they can be observed, and states a retirement condition for the query. It also names four open problems that have distinct failure conditions: closed citation loops that make root answers look orphaned, validity-biased selection pressure, signals that are unavailable at admission time, and the risk of Goodharting a composite score. Folding all of this into one paragraph would drop the boundary between lenses that work before retention and those that only work after it, and that boundary is what the cold-start problem depends on. The multi-section structure is justified.
